      "hints": [
        "Evaluate the range of $f(x) = \\frac{48}{x - 1}$ for $3 \\le x \\le 7$: $[8, 24]$.",
        "Ensure Range($f$) $\\subseteq [a, b]$, giving greatest $a = 8$ and least $b = 24$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Determine the range of $f(x) = \\frac{48}{x - 1}$ on the domain $[3, 7]$:\n$$f(7) = \\frac{48}{7 - 1} = \\frac{48}{6} = 8$$\n$$f(3) = \\frac{48}{3 - 1} = \\frac{48}{2} = 24$$\n$$\\text{Range of } f: \\quad [8, 24]$$",
        "For the composite function $gf$ to exist, the range of $f$ must be a subset of the domain of $g$, $[a, b]$:\n$$[8, 24] \\subseteq [a, b] \\implies a \\le 8 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b \\ge 24$$\n$$\\text{Greatest value of } a = 8, \\quad \\text{Least value of } b = 24$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Composite Function Existence": "States greatest $a = 8$ (B1) and least $b = 24$ (B1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
      }
